{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\uc1\htmautsp\deff2{\fonttbl{\f0\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f2\fcharset0 Arial;}}{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;}\loch\hich\dbch\pard\plain\ltrpar\itap0{\lang1033\fs18\f2\cf0 \cf0\ql{\f2 {\lang2057\ltrch The project will engage adults with support needs to engage in a programme of arts and culture in Leeds. Each group will participate in the planning and research of each visit. Digital skills will be embedded through research, planning and taking and uploading photographs and art work produced relating to each of the external visits. The project will promote culture and arts in the local area and the students will research and reflect on the accessibility in each venue as part of the project as related to individual needs. Students will participate in research and planning of all visits, developing digital skills, budgeting and planning skills aimed at improving independence. The project will develop a visitors guide aimed at promoting Leeds to a wider audience based on their experience. Delivery will be one week in class and one week on visits.\tab The project will take place at Swarthmore Centre and within the Leeds area, will be delivered each term for ten weeks. Alternate weeks will be in class / visiting places of interest. Locations for external visits will be discussed and guided through student participation and the sessions planned to ensure wider skills are developed. Team building, confidence, maths skills, planning, digital skills, travel confidence, budgeting will form part of the project.\tab }\li0\ri0\sa0\sb0\fi0\ql\par}
